<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Telkom deal may lop 1.2 bln rand off S.Africa debt.</title>
<headline>Telkom deal may lop 1.2 bln rand off S.Africa debt.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's sale of a 30 percent stake in Telkom for $1.261 billion or 5.58 billion rand could lop some 1.2 billion rand off state debt.</p>
<p>The government has committed to injecting 4.42 billion rand back into Telkom with the balance going to the state.</p>
<p>&quot;That balance will probably go to the reduction of debt,&quot; Posts, Telecommunications and Broadcasting Minister Jay Naidoo told Reuters.</p>
<p>South Africa has budgeted for a gross borrowing requirement of 36.85 billion rand in 1997/98.</p>
<p>The government is selling a 30 percent stake in Telkom to a consortium of SBC Communications Inc and Telekom Malaysia Bhd.</p>
<p>-- Ben Hirschler, Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
